#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:2
msgid "Snap deltas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:4
msgid ""
"A snap delta contains only the differences between one revision of a snap "
"and another. They're used to save bandwidth when downloading and uploading "
"snap package updates to the {ref}`Snap Store <ref-glossary_snap-store>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:6
msgid "Snap deltas come in two forms, _download_ deltas and _upload_ deltas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:8
msgid "Download deltas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:10
msgid ""
"Download deltas enable snap updates to be distributed in a bandwidth-"
"efficient manner, with no extra effort from the developer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:12
msgid ""
"Whenever a snap is released to a channel, the store automatically generates "
"a binary delta between the previously released snap revision and the newly "
"released snap revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:14
msgid ""
"Once the delta has been generated, clients with a sufficiently new snapd "
"will download the delta file instead of the full snap file of the revision "
"they're updating to. The downloaded delta will then be applied to the "
"client's existing snap and all assertions about the snap are verified by "
"snapd, which ensures that the client ends up with a snap that is bit-for-bit "
"identical to the snap it would have downloaded without the delta."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:16
msgid ""
"If the delta is too close in size to a full-size snap, it is discarded and a "
"full download is used instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:18
msgid ""
"Snap deltas are completely transparent to the developer and there is no way "
"to disable them. If a delta update is available, the delta will be "
"downloaded and applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:20
msgid "Download deltas are enabled by default in _snapd 2.23+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:22
msgid "Upload deltas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:24
msgid ""
"Upload deltas effectively use the same mechanism as download deltas, with "
"the main difference being that the delta is generated locally by Snapcraft "
"when a developer initiates an upload for a new version of their snap. The "
"delta contains only the differences between the most recently uploaded "
"revision and the new local revision. Once uploaded, the Snap Store applies "
"the delta to reconstruct the complete snap, verifying its integrity via its "
"digital signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:26
msgid "Saving space with deltas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:28
msgid ""
"The space savings provided by deltas vary depending on the size of the snap, "
"how often it gets updated, and how compressible the snap is (snaps that can "
"be compressed into a small size will benefit less from deltas than snaps "
"that are difficult to compress). In practice, the delta download size is "
"around 30% of the full snap size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/snap-deltas.md:30
msgid "The exact size of a delta can be determined with `snap refresh`."
msgstr ""
